### A1. The Multiplicity Mechanism in the Remark and Lean Source

*(Note: Mathematical claims of the Lean proof are `UNVERIFIED` as we do not build the repo; structural statements about what the `.lean` files define and assemble are `PROVED` by inspection.)*

1. **Analytic target (Landau positivity + Chebyshev nodes):**
   Top-level [Main.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Main.lean#L1-L12) and [MainConclusion.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/CharacterBoxes/MainConclusion.lean#L1-L14) deduce RH/GRH from bounding the Cesàro von Mangoldt remainder
   $$G_z(X) = \sum_{n \le X} \Lambda(n)\!\left(\frac{X}{n}-1\right) - X\log X + (1+\gamma)X \ll X^{\theta+\varepsilon}$$
   ([StatementOC.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/StatementOC.lean#L11-L30)). Discretizing a smoothed integral of $G_z$ over $m$ Chebyshev nodes `chebNode m j` has quadrature error $O(X \log m / m)$, forcing **$m \ge X^{1-\theta-\varepsilon}$** — hence **$m \asymp \sqrt{X}$** at $\theta = 1/2$ (`ZetaNonvanishingChebyshevWeights` in [ZetaNonvanishingChebyshevWeights.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/ZetaNonvanishingChebyshevWeights.lean#L9-L35), `FamilyLandauCW3` in [StatementFL.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/StatementFL.lean#L32-L43), `HalfSize` in [HalfLinks/Statement.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/HalfLinks/Statement.lean#L124-L127)).

2. **Base ($m=1$) local $p$-adic vanishing:**
   Fix a CM field $E/F$ containing an imaginary quadratic field $K = \mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{-d})$ (`Host` in [DataHost.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/LocalRingCardinality/DataHost.lean#L24-L68)). At a prime $p$ **inert** in $K$ (`InertK`), a CM curve/abelian variety has supersingular reduction of formal-group height 2: its formal logarithm has denominators $p^e$ only at degrees $p^{2e}$ (`letterLog` and `OneLetterR` in [GaussJetBounds/Statement.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/GaussJetBounds/Statement.lean#L74-L200), `ltLog` in [FormalGroupLog/Statement.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/FormalGroupLog/Statement.lean#L126-L135)). Differentiating an integral theta/CM function $a = X b$ times introduces $a!$, whose $p$-adic valuation $\frac{a}{p-1} - O(\log_p a)$ loses only $\rho(p)a = \frac{a}{p^2-1}$ to the height-2 logarithm (`OneLetterRadius`: $\gamma(p) - \frac{1}{p+1} = \rho(p)$), leaving net $p$-adic divisibility
   $$v_p\!\bigl(D^a \theta(0)\Omega^a\bigr) \;\ge\; \frac{p}{p^2-1}a - O(\log_p a) = \frac{a}{p} + \frac{a}{p^3} + \frac{a}{p^5} + \cdots - O(\log_p a).$$
   Truncated by Hodge/Fock weight $w_j \approx b$, each odd power $p^i \le X$ gains $\max(0, a/p^i - w_j)\log p \approx b(X/p^i - 1)_+\log p$ (`vonMangoldtClassSum` in [DataParams₂.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/LocalRingCardinality/DataParams₂.lean#L240-L243), `gainCM` in [StatementOCCM.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/ProductFormula/StatementOCCM.lean#L27-L32)) — directly encoding $\Lambda(p^i)(X/p^i - 1)$ into a $p$-adic valuation!

3. **Winning multiplicity $m$ via iterated theta lifts:**
   To sum $m$ shifted copies $\sum_{j=1}^m \max(0, a/p^i - w_j)$ while paying the evaluation degree $-a\log T$ at an auxiliary split prime $T \approx (bv/\pi)^m$ **only once**, they chain $m$ algebraic theta lifts (`ColumnChain.col` / `chainOpM` in [DataKernels.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/LocalRingCardinality/DataKernels.lean#L67-L76) and [ThetaLiftIndependence/Statement.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/ThetaLiftIndependence/Statement.lean#L52-L68)) across totally definite unitary groups $U(X_0) \to \dots \to U(X_m)$ of ranks $N_j = k + j(t+1)$ (`Spaces` in [DataSpaces.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/LocalRingCardinality/DataSpaces.lean#L77-L90)), adding Arthur/Speh summands $\pi \mapsto \pi \boxplus \mu_j[t]$. By Rallis inner-product and seesaw identities (`RallisAdj`, `DetChain`, `StepB` in [QuotientMetricDivisors/Statement.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/QuotientMetricDivisors/Statement.lean#L132-L193), `SiegelMassRatio` in [StatementMass.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/HermitianLattices/StatementMass.lean#L67-L89)), the Gram determinant factors across the $m$ lifts so local $p$-adic lattice indices **add** over $j=1,\dots,m$.

4. **Stepanov dictionary:**
   - *"Points" counted:* All inert prime powers $p^i \le X$ ($i$ odd).
   - *"Auxiliary polynomial":* The evaluation/Bessel-period map (`PeriodMap.PtilCol`, `DivisionInequalityWithCovolume` in [MeanHeightDescent/StatementJ.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/MeanHeightDescent/StatementJ.lean#L11-L62)) on $\mathcal{O}_K$-lattices of $m$-fold theta lifts, evaluated on order-$a$ CM jets at level $T$.
   - *Degree bound:* Bost's slope inequality (`SlopeInequality` in [LatticeSlopes/Statement.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/Formalism/LatticeSlopes/Statement.lean#L75-L82)) + Chowla–Selberg period mean (`ClassMean.Statement` in [ChowlaSelberg/Statements.lean](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-git/c1686473-142d-57cc-8202-223c6b26715f/scratchpad/leansrc/lean/src/GroundTheory/HeightsAndTheta/Heights/ChowlaSelberg/Statements.lean#L137-L142)).

