### A5. Verdict, Repo Barriers, Best Candidate + Missing Lemma, and Toy Test

- **Verdict: Clean kill.** Every translation into factoring lands in an established repo barrier:
  1. *Coppersmith/Arakelov lattice route:* Lands in **Lemma MI / Prop T** ([topblock_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/topblock_results.md#L310-L321)) and **§7 Q4** ([completeness_audit_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/completeness_audit_results.md#L296-L298)) — $n/4$ known bits / $N^{1/4}$ range; modulus-blind CM jets fail the single-prime product formula by $O(N^{-1/2})$.
  2. *Subexponential $X = L_N[\beta]$ theta-chain route:* Touches only $L_N[\beta]$-smooth primes, landing in **Theorem SS** ([suffmap_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/suffmap_results.md#L157-L195)).
  3. *Mod-$N$ CM-derivation route (`CM-Inert-Jet GCD`):* Pick $d$ with $\left(\frac{-d}{N}\right)=-1$, set $a = 4\lceil\sqrt{2N}/4\rceil+1$, output $\gcd(D^a s(0) \bmod N, N)$.
     - *Ledger:* $v_p(E_a) \ge 1$ (`PROVED`), $q \nmid E_a$ w.p. $1 - O(1/q)$ (`HEURISTIC`; `PROVED` at $a \equiv 1 \pmod{q-1}$), arithmetic cost $\tilde{O}(N^{1/2})$ via truncated ODE mod $N$.
     - *Single missing lemma for $L_N[\alpha < 1/3]$:* An $L_N[\alpha < 1/3]$-gate arithmetic straight-line program computing $E_a \bmod N$ at $a \asymp \sqrt{N}$. This lands directly in the **Pochhammer/SLP / $\tau$-conjecture barrier** ([suffmap_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/suffmap_results.md#L72-L73) Tier E; `slpcirc` Theorem SP in [BARRIERS.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/BARRIERS.md#L21-L22)) and **Theorem PT** ([BARRIERS.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/BARRIERS.md#L30-L31)).
- **Probability:** **$P(\alpha < 1/3\text{ heuristic}) < 0.1\%$.**

#### Pre-registered Toy Test ([prereg.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/multcopp_g/prereg.md), [toy_test.py](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/multcopp_g/toy_test.py))
Frozen before execution on $E: w^2 = 1 - s^4$ ($K = \mathbb{Q}(i)$, $E_a = D^a s(0) \in \mathbb{Z}$ for $a = 4k+1 \le 401$, plus pure mod-$N$ recurrence on 30 seeded 14–20-bit semiprimes with $\left(\frac{-1}{N}\right) = -1$):
- **P1 (Inert-prime multiplicity, `PASSED`):** $p \mid E_a$ for **481/481** pairs with $a \ge p$ ($p \in \{7,11,19,23,31\}$); $v_p(E_a) \ge \sum_{j\ge 0}\lfloor a/p^{2j+1}\rfloor - \lfloor\log_p a\rfloor - 1$ for **505/505** pairs. At $a=401, p=7$: $v_7(E_{401}) = 58 = \lfloor 401/7\rfloor + \lfloor 401/343\rfloor < v_7(401!) = 66$, confirming exact loss of the $\lfloor 401/7^2\rfloor = 8$ height-2 formal-log powers.
- **P2 (Split-prime periodicity, `PASSED`):** $E_{r+k(q-1)} \equiv A_q^k E_r \pmod q$ with $A_q \equiv (-1)^{(q-1)/4}\binom{(q-1)/2}{(q-1)/4} \not\equiv 0$ held in **505/505** cases ($q \in \{5,13,17,29,37\}$); $q \nmid E_{1+k(q-1)}$ in **188/188** cases.
- **P3 (Archimedean slope & Coppersmith ratio, `FAILED` on $\sqrt{2}$ constant / substantive $<1$ bound held):** $(\log|E_{401}| - (401\log 401 - 401))/401 = -0.6057$ vs. pre-registered $-\log\varpi = -0.2708$, because the nearest poles of $\operatorname{sl}(u)$ lie at $(1\pm i)\varpi$ of modulus $\sqrt{2}\varpi$ ($-\log(\sqrt{2}\varpi) = -0.6174$, post-hoc gap $0.012$); likewise $\max \frac{v_p(E_a)\log p}{\log|E_a|} = 0.3136$ (at tiny $a$, vs. pre-registered $0.15$), still bounded strictly away from $1$ ($< 0.04$ for $a \ge 100$).
- **P4 (Mod-$N$ hidden-factor test, `PASSED`):** At Coppersmith scale $a_{\text{low}} \approx N^{1/4} < p$, $\gcd(E_{a_{\text{low}}} \bmod N, N) = p$ succeeded **0/30** times; at $a_{\text{high}} \approx \sqrt{2N} > p$, pure mod-$N$ recurrence yielded $\gcd(E_{a_{\text{high}}} \bmod N, N) = p$ in **30/30** cases — confirming both the hidden-$p$ CM separation and the hard $a \ge p \asymp \sqrt{N}$ wall.
